{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lin, one of the psychiatry team doctors. I’m here to talk with you after your visit to the ER. Can you tell me what happened yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I was driving from my boyfriend’s place to get coffee. Out of nowhere, I just felt this overwhelming urge to end it. I pressed the gas all the way down and left it for about a minute."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really intense. Did you plan to crash the car?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought about swerving, but I didn’t. I just… let go of the gas and slowed down. I don’t even know why I stopped. I guess part of me didn’t want to do it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you’re here and safe. You mentioned feeling like a burden. Can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:20:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I feel like everyone would be better off without me. My mom, my boyfriend, my brother—they’re always worrying. I’m a new mom, but I don’t feel like I’m doing a good job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:21:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Having a baby is hard, especially with everything else you’re managing. You’ve been through a lot—bipolar disorder, ECT, chronic pain. That’s not easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s exhausting. I’ve been doing ECT weekly, but I still feel so low. And the pain from endometriosis doesn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure your pain is managed. Right now, your safety is our top priority. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to hurt myself. But the thoughts just come out of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with bipolar and borderline personality disorder. We’re going to keep you here for a few days to monitor you and adjust your treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to keep doing ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve scheduled your next session for Friday. It’s part of your ongoing care. We’ll continue it here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. It helps, even if it’s not a cure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also check your thyroid levels. You’re on medication for hypothyroidism, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:29:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, levothyroxine. I take it every morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-09-12 20:30:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure that’s optimized. Low thyroid can worsen depression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How did you sleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not great. I kept waking up. My stomach pain flared up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll adjust your pain meds. Gabapentin and tramadol are still working for you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:18:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They help a little, but not enough on bad days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll increase the gabapentin slightly and see how you respond. Also, your labs came back—thyroid levels are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-09-13 08:20:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried it might be off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-09-14 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today emotionally?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-09-14 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still down. I had a moment this morning where I thought, ‘Why not just end it?’ But I called the nurse instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-09-14 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was really strong of you. Reaching out is exactly what we want. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-09-14 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just feel so guilty. My baby needs me, but I can’t even take care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-09-14 10:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Postpartum stress, bipolar, chronic pain—it’s a lot. But you’re doing the right thing by being here and getting help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-09-15 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ECT session is scheduled for noon today. Any questions before we go in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-09-15 11:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it normal to feel groggy afterward?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-09-15 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, most people feel a bit drowsy for a few hours. We’ll monitor you closely after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-09-15 13:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well today. The seizure was adequate. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-09-15 13:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired. Headache. But not confused, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-09-15 13:47:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you something for the headache. Keep drinking water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-09-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any suicidal thoughts since the ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-09-16 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Less intense. Still there, but quieter. I didn’t feel the urge to act on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-09-16 09:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. ECT often helps reduce those impulses over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-09-17 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s your mood today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-09-17 08:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. I smiled at my baby’s picture. That felt… real."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-09-17 08:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s really meaningful. Small moments like that are important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-09-18 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ready for your second ECT session?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-09-18 11:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah. I’m hoping it helps even more this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-09-18 13:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Session went well. You’re responding as expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-09-18 13:51:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay. Just sleepy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-09-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any thoughts of self-harm today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-09-19 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I’ve been thinking about my son. I want to be here for him."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-09-19 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a powerful reason to keep going. We’re seeing real improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your asthma and reflux are stable. Still using your inhaler as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, just once or twice a week. The reflux is better since I’ve been eating smaller meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Keep that up. We’re planning your discharge for Friday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Discharge? Where will I go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re arranging transfer to an inpatient psychiatric facility for continued ECT and therapy. It’s a step down, but still supportive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-09-20 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m nervous, but I think I need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-09-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-09-21 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More stable. I’ve been journaling. It helps me process things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-09-21 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Journaling can be a powerful tool. Keep using it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-09-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s your last day here. You’ll have one more ECT session at noon before transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-09-22 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. I feel like I’m in a better place than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-09-22 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made real progress. You’re safer, more connected to your reasons for living, and responding to treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-09-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final ECT session went well. You’re doing great. The transport team will take you to the psychiatric facility in an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-09-22 12:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I know I’m not ‘fixed,’ but I feel like I can keep fighting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-09-22 12:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly the goal. Keep reaching out, keep showing up. You’re not alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-09-22 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll miss the team here, but I’m ready for the next step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-09-22 13:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll miss you too. But this isn’t goodbye—it’s part of your journey. Keep in touch with your care team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-09-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Transport is here. You’ve done really well. Stay strong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2172-09-22 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-09-12 19:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-09-22 15:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 34-year-old woman was admitted after reporting a self-aborted suicide attempt involving accelerating her car without veering off the road. She endorsed passive suicidal ideation and feelings of being a burden to her family. During her 10-day psychiatric admission, she continued her weekly bilateral ECT sessions on days 3, 6, and 10, with gradual improvement in mood and reduction in suicidal thoughts. Her chronic conditions—hypothyroidism, endometriosis-related pain, asthma, and GERD—were monitored and managed with stable medications. She engaged in care, expressed connection to her infant child as a protective factor, and demonstrated improved emotional stability. She was discharged to an inpatient psychiatric facility for ongoing ECT and therapy, alert, cooperative, and with a reinforced safety plan.",
    "problems": [
      "Bipolar disorder, unspecified",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Endometriosis, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated"
    ]
  }
}
